course: dictionary
lesson: 2988
title: Context clues about a gentle sea cow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary is useful, but you can often work out a new word from the words around it. This is called context. The sentence «Dugongs graze on sea grass like underwater cows» tells you a lot: dugongs eat sea grass, and they are compared to cows that live underwater.
explain: Look for clues. A dugong is a large sea mammal that eats plants, so it is not a fish. Mammal means an animal with warm blood that feeds its babies milk, and the dugong is a relative of the manatee. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then try your idea in place of the hard word to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one name. «Dugongs are sea cows» uses another name for the dugong. When a writer tells you a word is like something you already know, that is a clue: the new word means something like the familiar one, but in the sea.
fact: A dugong is a large, gentle sea mammal with a whale-like tail.
fact: Dugongs live in warm, shallow seas and graze on sea grass.
fact: Because they eat sea grass like cows eat grass on land, dugongs are called sea cows.
fact: The manatee is a relative of the dugong.
fact: Long ago, sailors may have mistaken dugongs and manatees for mermaids.
exercise: «Dugongs graze on sea grass like underwater cows.» What does graze mean here? | Sleep under rocks | Swim very fast | *Eat grass slowly | Jump out of the sea
exercise: «Steller's sea cow had no teeth; hard rough plates in its mouth crushed soft seaweed.» What does crushed mean? | Swallowed whole | Painted bright colours | *Squashed into small pieces | Tickled gently
exercise: What is a dugong? | *A large, gentle sea mammal with a whale-like tail | A rock that floats on the sea | A small fish with sharp spines | A bird that flies low over the waves
test: Which animal is a living relative of the dugong? | Penguin | Crab | *Manatee | Shark
test: «Sailors long ago may have mistaken dugongs and manatees for mermaids.» What might sailors have mistaken dugongs for? | Octopuses | Sharks | *Mermaids | Whales
exam: What kind of seas do dugongs live in? | Frozen lakes | Rivers far inland | Cold, deep oceans | *Warm, shallow seas
